I don't know why you experienced this; from the source and wizard mode 
tests, the recharge counter on tools is ignored (except for magic 
markers).  You have to empty the horn each time to get the best effect, 
but I'm guessing you knew that.

Even getting 6-15 charges per useful invocation, it'll be close.
Only 1 in 13 of those charges yields a potion; roughly 2 in 5 of the
potions are fruit juice or booze.  Each of those is 600 more turns of 
life.  My preliminary tests indicate that, most of the time, that's not 
enough.  

In particular I simulated getting the factory set up with 1000 
turns to live, then invoking every 80 turns.  (Which is a little 
suboptimal.)  Then I ask, what happens first, death or getting the 
turns-of-life up to 10000 turns?

If I just drink the fruit juice and booze, I die 4/5 of the time.
If I cancel and/or dilute the other potions, though,
I live 5/7 of the time.  I think with polypiling I can do even
better.

All of this is moot, of course, if I can't get the PYEC and a horn of 
plenty by turn 12000 or so. :)  Since I often reach the castle around 
turn 40000, this will require a significant change in playing style.

